thread:
Ivy (CS): Ethan reported a burst of 429s during onboarding for their mobile web app. Attaching short trace excerpts.
Ethan (Client): on Android webview we see many failures right after resume from background. Token TTL is 25s.
Noah (SE): interesting — do you re-fetch tokens on visibilitychange or on reconnect? that can amplify bursts if many tabs/resumes happen.
Ethan (Client): our service-worker tries to revalidate session on 'online' event and we call getToken() then immediately kick off a batch of API calls. code: 
```js
self.addEventListener('sync', async () => {
 const t = await fetch('/token').then(r=>r.json()).token;
 clients.matchAll().then(c => c.forEach(client => client.postMessage({type:'TOKEN', token: t})));
});
```
Ethan (Client): so multiple clients receive the token and do concurrent requests; but tokens expire quickly so some tabs re-request in parallel.
Ivy (CS): that pattern can create a stampede especially with service workers that fanout to clients.
Kira (SRE): our per-key throttle detects high short-window concurrency and enforces conservative limits for TTL <30s. That aligns with the traces. We can help two ways: recommend client change or provide a temporary quota increase while you roll out fixes.
Noah (SE): client quick fixes: 1) move token minting into a singleflight inside the service-worker so only one network mint runs; 2) add small local cache with expiry buffer; 3) add exponential jitter on 429 responses. Example inside SW: 
```js
let inflight = null;
async function mint(){
 if(inflight) return inflight;
 inflight = fetch('/token').then(r=>r.json()).finally(()=> inflight = null);
 return inflight;
}
```
Ethan (Client): we also have a bug where visibilitychange triggers a full reconnect and revalidation even when token still valid — we'll patch to check expiry before requesting.
Kira (SRE): temporary measure: increase per-key rate for onboarding. QuotaBot: updated customer=Heliotrope key=mobile-123 old=150/min new=900/min expires=18h.
QuotaBot: change applied by Kira.
Ethan (Client): deployed SW singleflight + expiry-check to alpha group; 429s dropped from ~10% to ~0.8% on resume tests. A few flakes remain when users spam reopen.
Noah (SE): for longer term, consider issuance of 10m session tokens for mobile web with audience-scoped constraints, or use bounded refresh tokens so the SPA isn't minting per-request. We'll add a note to integration docs.
Ivy (CS): I'll schedule a short enablement with the mobile engs to walk through service-worker patterns and TTL tradeoffs.
Kira (SRE): left an entry in the account notes about the temporary bump; will revert after 18h unless you request extension.
Ethan (Client): thanks all, big improvement. Will monitor metrics and report if anything resurfaces :thumbsup:
